script = ExtResource("1_page")
id = &"first-minutes"
title = "Your first minutes"
order = 20
summary = "You start with two squads and no base. Only one of them can found it."
body = "You begin with exactly two squads and no buildings.

Your GATHERER CREW is the one that matters first. It is the only squad that
can found your town centre — and founding SPENDS it. One crew, one town. It
also works resource nodes, which is the rest of its life.

Your GENERAL cannot build anything at all. He is a fighting squad, and his
presence steadies troops around him. Ordering him to build is refused, and
that refusal is the commonest way a first match quietly goes wrong: the clock
runs while your economy has not started.

The selection panel says which is which, and the line under your resources
names the squad to use until a town centre stands.

## In order

- Select the crew and place a town centre. Choose ground with trees and food in reach — you cannot move it afterwards.
- The crew builds the hall and walks into it when the work is done. While it builds it takes no other orders — one crew, one town, so you cannot found a second while the first is going up.
- The town centre trains more gatherer crews. Send them at nodes.
- A barracks lets you train soldiers, and it costs wood. Wood first.
- Scout with the general meanwhile. You cannot fight what you have not found, and you cannot plan around a neighbour you have not located.

What everything costs is on the Buildings and Troops pages, which read it out
of the game's own data rather than out of this sentence.

## If you lose your town

Any gatherer crew can found a new one. Being razed is not being eliminated —
see \"Winning and losing\"."
